# Unity YAML assets: merge with Unity's SmartMerge (UnityYAMLMerge) instead of
# git's line-based text merge. Git diffs these as lines, so moving an object
# within a scene reads as a huge conflict; SmartMerge parses them into Unity's
# object graph and merges per-object, so reordering stops mattering.
#
# Deliberately limited to scenes and prefabs. Do NOT widen this to *.asset or
# *.meta: git hands merge drivers extensionless temp files, so UnityYAMLMerge
# cannot match its own extension rules and always falls through to the tool list
# in mergespecfile.txt. If none of those tools is installed, it aborts the WHOLE
# merge with an opaque error rather than leaving conflict markers. Settings and
# .meta files are simple key/value YAML that git merges fine on its own, and a
# visible conflict there beats a fatal one.
#
# The driver is defined per-machine, since the path to UnityYAMLMerge.exe differs
# per install. Each developer needs this in their own .git/config:
#
#   [merge "unityyamlmerge"]
#       name = Unity SmartMerge
#       driver = '<path-to>/UnityYAMLMerge.exe' merge -p %O %B %A %A
#
# Without it, git warns the driver is undefined and falls back to the normal
# text merge - no breakage, just no benefit.

*.unity   merge=unityyamlmerge
*.prefab  merge=unityyamlmerge
